The primeFactors() method iteratively checks every number up to the number itself to see if it is a prime factor. It does this by dividing the number by the checked number and checks if the remainder is 0 - if it is, then it is a prime factor. The checked number is added to the HashSet, and the number itself is divided by the checked number to reduce the number. 

Finally, the method returns the HashSet containing all the unique prime factors of the number.

