Below is the corrected function. It uses two additional variables "lastIndex" and "count" to hold the index of the last element that satisfies the condition and the count of such elements respectively.

```javascript
function findLast(arr, func) {
    let last = null;
    let lastIndex = -1;
    let count = 0;

    for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (func(arr[i])) {
            last = arr[i];
            lastIndex = i;
            count++;
        }
    }
